%I A400380 #38 Nov 06 2026 04:25:40
%S A400380 146,218,410,530,818,1370,2330,3218,3890,5018,6290,8210,9818,11570,
%T A400380 14810,20018,21650,22490,24218,35930,47450,51218,57818,61970,75290,
%U A400380 76850,102170,105818,111410,129050,135218,141530,150170,156818,192218,197210,223130,245018,253490,273818,282770,298010
%N A400380 Sum of squares of the n-th sexy prime pair (p, p+6).
%C A400380 All terms after the first end in 0 or 8. (Proof: for p > 5, p cannot be congruent to 9 mod 10, since then p+6 would be divisible by 5 and greater than 5. Hence p == 1, 3, or 7 mod 10, giving a(n) == 0, 0, or 8 mod 10 respectively).
%H A400380 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400380/b400380.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400380 a(n) = p^2 + (p+6)^2 where p = A023201(n).
%F A400380 a(n) == 2 (mod 24).
%e A400380 a(1) = 5^2 + 11^2 = 25 + 121 = 146.
%e A400380 a(2) = 7^2 + 13^2 = 49 + 169 = 218.
%e A400380 a(3) = 11^2 + 17^2 = 121 + 289 = 410.
%t A400380 Map[#^2 + (# + 6)^2 &, Select[Prime[Range[100]], PrimeQ[# + 6] &]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 06 2026 *)
%Y A400380 Cf. A023201.
%K A400380 nonn,easy,new
%O A400380 1,1
%A A400380 _Dylan Gardiner_, Oct 30 2026
